  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Rad Saturation" id="59d4-4d8e-5865-624e" hidden="false">
      <description>While an enemy Biological unit is Engaged with a unit with this rule, they reduce their Toughness by 1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Enhanced Data-Tether (X)" id="eb4f-d5e2-48c8-a67c" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit which contains a model with an Enhanced Data-Tether (X) can use up to X Binheric Dice in a single Override. If it contains multiple models with this equipment, they can still only use a single Override per activation. An Enhanced Data-Tether (X) can be used once per phase in the Action or Combat phases.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Broad Spectrum Data-Tether" id="8307-faea-1acb-3334" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit which is within 6” of a model with a Broad Spectrum Data-Tether can use up to 1 Binheric Dice in a single Override. A Broad Spectrum Data-Tether can only be used once per turn, and only in the Action phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Omnispex" id="2915-c21f-8067-1302" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit which contains a model with an Omnispex ignores the effect of Stealth when targeting units.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
  <rules>
    <rule name="Binheric Overrides" id="b4f6-9710-14c3-2e13" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of the battle, roll 10 d6, keep track of the order and results. These are called Binheric Dice.


Models within range of a Data-Tether can utilise an Override once per activation. To do so, select the next Binheric Dice from the stack and replace a rolled To Hit or To Wound dice with it. After using an Override, roll one d6 and add it to the end of the override stack. Binheric Dice added to the override stack cannot be used until the following turn.
Enhanced Data-Tether - the unit may use 1 override die
Datasmith - the unit may use 1 override die
Marshal, Technoarchaeologist, Enginseer, Manipulus - the unit may use 2 override dice
Dominus - the unit may use 3 override dice</description>
      <alias>Binheric Dice</alias>
    </rule>
  </rules>
</catalogue>
